Key Findings – Research Paper 2 (Crowley et al., 2020)
The paper outlines a vision for a more equitable and accessible U.S. healthcare system, emphasising universal coverage.

It highlights that high healthcare costs remain a major barrier preventing many Americans from receiving necessary care.

The authors argue that the current system suffers from inefficiencies, fragmentation, and inconsistent quality across different populations.

They emphasise the need for policy reforms to expand coverage, reduce financial burdens, and improve affordability.

The study stresses that cost transparency and better regulation are essential for controlling rising healthcare expenses.

It identifies disparities in access and outcomes, showing that vulnerable groups face greater challenges in obtaining care.

The paper proposes a framework for improving coverage and cost management to create a fairer, more sustainable healthcare system.
